# F4: F3 with the four-card QUAD on (one 64-row batched draft over the pool live banks): the quad reads the active banks and copies only when a device bank is on the spare side. Audited, NOT timed. SOFT: stop only if the quad itself fails, as in the batched-draft window; then the target is pairs + fused commit + live banks (F3 and the F5 pairs arms).
# Duration (estimate): 25 / 50 / 90 min as F2.
# Read: the launched-argv line (the profile's QWEN_FAST_FUSED_COMMIT=1, _INPLACE=1 and the flags each step names); ONE engaged line '[PACKED-FUSED] ... users=4 rows=16 inplace=1 ... kernel=direct traces=68 layout=1x80'; every '[PACKED-FUSED-AUDIT]' line checked=80 mismatches=0, one per fused publication (audits == fused publications); today-path lines ('path=today reason=R') only with R in ramp or parity; no discard, no 'fused commit refused', no '[PINDIAG] fused commit audit mismatch'; coherent text. c2_smoke_check.py applies these rules and fails the run on them; plus in concurrent4_steady exactly ONE '[PINDIAG] quad draft engaged slots=[0,1,2,3] ... live_banks=1', '[QUAD-DRAFT] round=N' per round, every '[DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] ... equal=1', no '[QUAD-DRAFT] fallback' and no '[PINDIAG] quad draft disabled'.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card fused-commit window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fcommit and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are
# the driver's, on the allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image F0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver picks.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-fcommit-quad
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
